  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 254 AM MDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nOn Sunday, we can expect slight ridging over the area. The\nregion will likely be between the remnants of Hurricane Isaias\nand a large trough over the western United States. With this\nsetup we will likely be above average temperatures in the low to\nmid 80s. Winds are forecast to be from the southwest at 15 to 20\nmph. With the upper-level southwest flow, a few clouds should\npass over the area with the mid- to upper-level moisture moving\nthrough.\n\nFor Monday through Thursday, the upper-level trough swings\nthrough from the southwest that could potentially bring in a\ncold front Wednesday afternoon and Thursday morning. This\npattern should bring chances of showers into the area. with the\nchances of showers, it is unclear exactly where and when these\nshowers will be. However, the showers will likely be light over\nthe area. Temperatures are forecast to be in the 70s and then\n60s. There is some uncertainty with the timing of the cold front\nas it could either slow down or speed up. If the cold front\nslows down, we could expect showers to be later in Thursday with\nwarmer temperatures. However, if the cold front speeds up we\nwill have showers much earlier than expected with the majority\nof the showers happening on Wednesday and cooler temperatures.",
